3054.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/agra-court-grants-bail-to-6-cong-workers-arrested-for-defacing-cec-gyanesh-kumars-ancestral-home/articleshow/134663054.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T22:12:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134663104,imgsize-1043240.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Helicopters, influencers and nail art: The money trail of 2026 assembly elections]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/helicopters-influencers-and-nail-art-the-money-trail-of-2026-assembly-elections/articleshow/134662872.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134662872.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The BJP and Congress have filed their election expenditure reports following several assembly elections this year. The BJP recorded a hefty expenditure of Rs 529.39 crore across five states, whereas Congress spent Rs 248.55 crore. These contrasting figures unveil the distinct priorities of the political parties, particularly in West Bengal and Keralam.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/helicopters-influencers-and-nail-art-the-money-trail-of-2026-assembly-elections/articleshow/134662872.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/helicopters-influencers-and-nail-art-the-money-trail-of-2026-assembly-elections/articleshow/134662872.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T22:09:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Arghya Prasun Roychowdhury</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134663102,imgsize-135646.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Akhilesh Yadav asks SP leaders to keep seat-sharing concerns internal amid friction with Congress]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/akhilesh-yadav-asks-sp-leaders-to-keep-seat-sharing-concerns-internal-amid-friction-with-congress/articleshow/134662978.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134662978.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Akhilesh Yadav, president of the Samajwadi Party, encouraged leaders to express seat-sharing concerns privately. Tensions arose after Shiv Pal Singh Patel criticized Congress' demand for 150 seats in upcoming elections. Patel emphasized that Congress should receive a more realistic allocation based on their previous performance. Uttar Pradesh Congress president Aradhana Mishra stated that top leadership will decide the seat allocation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/akhilesh-yadav-asks-sp-leaders-to-keep-seat-sharing-concerns-internal-amid-friction-with-congress/articleshow/134662978.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/akhilesh-yadav-asks-sp-leaders-to-keep-seat-sharing-concerns-internal-amid-friction-with-congress/articleshow/134662978.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T22:07:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134663004,imgsize-46646.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Example of their frustration': Shivraj Singh Chouhan slams Congress for calling Modi 'illegal' PM]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/example-of-their-frustration-shivraj-singh-chouhan-slams-congress-for-calling-modi-illegal-pm/articleshow/134662619.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134662619.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.c